simpledrm: sync updates to the scanout's line counter

simpledrm copies every update straight into the buffer the display
controller is scanning out; when the copy and the scanout cross, the
picture tears horizontally (plain while scrolling). With an optional
scanout-line-count-reg property, the physical address of the
controller's current-line counter (INTF_LINE_COUNT of the DPU's INTF_1
here), wait for the counter to wrap before copying, so the copy starts in
the vertical blanking and stays ahead of the scanout. The counter is
checked at probe (it must wrap at a steady 4-50 ms per frame), otherwise
the sync stays off.

